cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata in CITATION.cff."
type: software

title: "SE Verification: Self-Similarity"

authors:
  - family-names: Case
    given-names: Denise M.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6165-7389"
    affiliation: "Northwest Missouri State University, School of Computer Science and Information Systems, Maryville, MO, USA"

repository-code: "https://github.com/structural-explainability/se-verification-self-similarity"
url: "https://github.com/structural-explainability/se-verification-self-similarity"
license: MIT

abstract: >
  Independent Lean 4 mathematical verification testbed for
  Structural Explainability (SE) individuation, co-reference,
  and persistence. The project studies self-similar mathematical
  constructions, including symbolic coding, distinct presentations
  of identical points, finite-word transformations, and attractor
  invariance under changes to probability weights. It develops
  formal examples and counterexamples to examine the mathematical
  consequences and scientific interpretation boundaries of
  canonical SE theory definitions. The repository separates
  mathematical verification from empirical validation and
  does not define new foundational identity criteria.

keywords:
  - structural-explainability
  - formal-verification
  - lean4
  - mathematical-testbed
  - counterexamples
  - self-similarity
  - individuation
  - coreference
  - persistence
  - identity
  - reproducibility
